WEBVTT

00:05:59.333 --> 00:06:00.737
who had nearly died in prison

00:06:00.761 --> 00:06:03.791
and had spent many years
in solitary confinement,

00:06:03.815 --> 00:06:09.771
told me she was grateful to her jailers
for the time she had had to think,

00:06:09.795 --> 00:06:11.897
for the wisdom she had gained,

00:06:11.921 --> 00:06:15.080
for the chance to hone
her meditation skills.

00:06:15.861 --> 00:06:17.405
She had sought meaning

00:06:17.429 --> 00:06:20.649
and made her travail
into a crucial identity.

00:06:21.458 --> 00:06:25.299
But if the people I met
were less bitter than I'd anticipated

00:06:25.323 --> 00:06:26.860
about being in prison,

00:06:26.884 --> 00:06:29.725
they were also less thrilled
than I'd expected

00:06:29.749 --> 00:06:32.813
about the reform process
going on in their country.